<title>UK: BOE gives money mkt 400 mln stg help at set rates.</title>
<headline>BOE gives money mkt 400 mln stg help at set rates.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said that it provided the UK money market with 400 million stg of assistance at established interest rates to help with a forecast shortage of 1.7 billion stg.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1100 GMT   1300 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.7 BLN    =	    =	    =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    400 MLN!   =	    =	    =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 400 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING IN EQUAL AMOUNTS ON OCT 21</p>
<p>&amp; 22 AT 5-23/32 PCT</p>
<p>(INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
